WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:03.400
When it comes to something
as life-and-death important

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.120
as what to feed ourselves
and our families,

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:10.760
we should rely not on
anecdotes, but on facts.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:13.040
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast.

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:16.320
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:20.120
Nearly two million women in the U.S.
will enter menopause this year.

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:22.400
So what does the research tell us

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:25.680
about the best methods to alleviate
menopausal symptoms?

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:28.120
Here’s our first story.

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:30.400
Testosterone is linked
with sexual desire

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.600
in both men and women.

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:34.560
Women normally produce
testosterone

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:36.120
throughout the life cycle.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:38.080
Although postmenopausal ovaries

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:39.920
continue to produce
testosterone,

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:42.800
levels naturally decline
with age.

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:44.440
Testosterone blood levels
decrease

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:47.120
approximately 50 percent
by age 50,

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:49.640
which may play a role
in the decline in libido

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:53.480
(using masturbation frequency
as a partner-independent proxy).

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:57.200
A syndrome of "female androgen
deficiency" symptoms

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:58.880
has been popularized,

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:01.960
but there is no evidence
testosterone "replacement"

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:04.480
helps with mood or well-being,
hot flashes,

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:07.640
or bone, cardiovascular,
or metabolic health.

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:10.800
The only evidence-based reason
to try testosterone

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:12.400
in postmenopausal women

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:14.840
is for the treatment
of low sexual desire

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:16.680
that causes distress.

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:18.480
A systematic review
and meta-analysis

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:20.560
of three dozen
randomized controlled trials

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:22.840
involving more than 8,000 women

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:24.480
found that
testosterone treatment

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:28.520
significantly increased
postmenopausal sexual desire.

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:32.200
The increase in frequency
of "satisfactory sexual events"

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:34.360
was statistically significant,

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.640
but not
clinically significant enough

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:38.640
to warrant FDA approval,

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:40.560
especially given
the uncertainty

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:42.760
about long-term side effects.

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:45.680
The women on testosterone
only logged a little under

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:48.920
one additional satisfactory
sexual event a month,

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:50.560
compared to placebo.

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:52.200
Currently,
there are more than 30

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:55.240
FDA-approved
testosterone products for men,

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:57.000
but none for women.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:58.920
Clinicians can trial
a few months

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:02.240
of a male transdermal
testosterone preparation

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:04.480
at one-tenth the dose or less,

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:07.000
making sure to check levels
to prevent overdosing,

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:09.720
which can have
virilizing side effects,

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:12.760
such as clitoral enlargement
and voice changes.

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:15.960
Even at premenopausal
physiological doses,

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:18.400
testosterone can cause acne
and excessive hair growth

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:20.800
on the chin, cheeks,
and upper lip.

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:22.960
Unlike oral testosterone,

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:25.360
formulations administered
through the skin

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:27.360
don't appear to have
the same negative effects

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:28.960
on cholesterol levels,

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:31.080
but long-term safety data
for women

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:32.840
regarding cardiovascular,
cancer,

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:35.920
and cognitive outcomes
are lacking.

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:36.680
It has been estimated

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:38.840
that more than a fifth
of prescriptions

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:42.840
for male testosterone products
are actually written for women,

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:46.720
and this is not including
custom-compounded testosterone.

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:48.240
A consensus position statement

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:50.080
of international
medical societies

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:51.560
specializing in hormone issues

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:55.560
recommends against compounded
"bioidentical" testosterone

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:58.880
due to the lack of evidence
for efficacy and safety.

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:02.240
Similarly,
the dietary supplement DHEA,

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:04.400
which can convert
into testosterone

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:05.440
within the body,

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:08.360
cannot be recommended
for low libido in women,

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:09.520
since a meta-analysis

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:11.600
of more than 20
randomized controlled trials

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:13.560
found no significant effect

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:16.680
on improving desire
and sexual function.

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:18.240
Are there any natural ways

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:21.120
for women to raise
their testosterone levels?

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:23.960
Listening to music
for just 30 minutes

00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:26.240
can increase testosterone levels
in young women

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:28.720
by about 20 percent.

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:29.320
Interestingly,

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:32.400
the opposite effect
was found in men.

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:33.800
For more
on the effects of music,

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:38.640
check out
my video Music as Medicine.

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:42.600
Heavy mint consumption
can lower testosterone levels

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:44.040
in both men and women.

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:46.840
There are case reports of men
drinking four cups (0.95 L)

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:48.560
a day of spearmint
or peppermint tea

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:50.920
losing their sex drive.

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:53.760
Given the apparent
anti-androgenic effects,

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:55.440
researchers decided
to try it out

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:58.360
on women concerned
about excessive hairiness,

00:03:58.360 --> 00:04:00.000
and in a matter
of just five days,

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.120
were able to drop
their free testosterone levels

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:03.200
by about 30 percent

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:06.000
with two cups (0.50 L)
of mint tea a day.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:09.880
There's a syndrome called PCOS,
or polycystic ovarian syndrome,

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:12.480
which can result in abnormally
high testosterone levels

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:13.520
in women,

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:16.920
which can be successfully
brought down with mint tea,

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:19.000
but for women
struggling with low libido,

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:22.920
it might not be
a good choice.

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:23.680
In my next story,

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:28.025
we look at the different health risks
of vaginal and oral estrogen.

00:04:28.025 --> 00:04:28.960
I explained
how the first-line treatment

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:32.920
for mild to moderate vaginal dryness
due to menopause are lubricants

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:34.080
and moisturizers, and I called out
the safest brands.

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:37.400
If over-the-counter lubricants
and moisturizers are insufficient

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:41.160
to control the genitourinary
symptoms of menopause, low-dose,

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:43.840
local estrogen therapy
is recommended,

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:46.640
unless women have a history
of hormone-dependent cancers

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:48.720
like endometrial or breast.

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:52.880
Local, meaning applied vaginally,
as opposed to taken orally.

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:55.800
Vaginal application is considered
safer and more effective

00:04:55.800 --> 00:04:57.880
than systemic hormone therapy.

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:00.800
A meta-analysis of 58 studies
comparing vaginal

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:04.680
to systemic estrogens
found that vaginal estrogen therapy

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:08.720
offered better symptom relief
than estrogen pills, patches, or implants.

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:12.760
In fact, many women who are on systemic
menopausal hormone therapy

00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:17.600
have to add on supplemental vaginal
estrogens to control symptoms.

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:20.400
Vaginal estrogens are available
as a variety of creams,

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:22.200
suppositories, and rings.

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:25.440
Thirty randomized, control comparative
trials have been performed,

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:28.080
and there appears to be
no difference in efficacy

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:29.640
between the various preparations.

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:33.720
However, they may take weeks
before a noticeable alleviation

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:36.200
of symptoms is detected,
and two to three months

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:38.800
before the full effect is achieved.

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:41.440
Although year-long studies
can clearly demonstrate

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:44.760
vaginal estrogen’s benefit,
studies as long as 12 weeks

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:48.680
have failed to manifest
superiority to placebo.

00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:51.160
Some of the estrogen applied
to the vulva or vagina

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:54.120
is systemically absorbed
and therefore convey

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:58.080
the same black box FDA notice
that oral estrogens carry,

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:01.200
an all-caps warning of increased risk
of “endometrial cancer,

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:04.800
cardiovascular disorders, breast cancer
and probable dementia.”

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:07.320
Vaginal estrogen
is considered safer, though,

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:09.920
since it can be used
at a much lower dose

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:12.880
(as low as one-hundredth the oral dose).

00:06:12.880 --> 00:06:16.360
The Harvard Nurse’s Health Study
did not find any increased risks

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:20.400
associated with vaginal estrogen use
over 18 years of follow-up.

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:22.640
Randomized controlled trials
lasting up to a year

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:24.640
appear to confirm its safety,

00:06:24.640 --> 00:06:28.480
but there have been observational
studies linking vaginal use

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:31.560
to about a doubling of odds
for endometrial cancer,

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:33.720
but this was done
back in the 1970s

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:35.800
when higher estrogen doses
were used.

00:06:35.800 --> 00:06:38.720
And a more recent study out of Denmark
that found the same thing

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:42.680
may have been confounded
by concurrent oral estrogen exposure.

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:45.040
Out of an abundance of caution, though,

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:48.760
even low-dose localized estrogen
may be contraindicated

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:52.640
in hormone-dependent cancer survivors
to be on the safe side.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:55.120
Breast cancer survivors
suffering from GSM

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:58.880
may want to consider
vaginal DHEA instead.

00:06:58.880 --> 00:07:02.560
Oral DHEA doesn’t appear
to offer any benefit,

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:07.040
but in 2016 the FDA approved vaginal
DHEA suppositories for pain

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:09.600
during intercourse due to menopause.

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:11.880
It’s converted locally into estrogen

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:15.640
and does not significantly
affect systemic hormone levels.

00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:18.840
A downside is that it has to be
administered nightly,

00:07:18.840 --> 00:07:21.360
whereas estrogen preparations
are typically twice a week,

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:24.600
or even every few months
with the vaginal rings.

00:07:24.600 --> 00:07:27.120
For those who would rather
have an oral treatment,

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:30.040
there is ospemifene,
a tamoxifen-type drug

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:33.840
that has pro-estrogenic effects
on the vaginal lining.

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:36.320
However, it can actually double
the rate of hot flashes

00:07:36.320 --> 00:07:38.760
and urinary tract infections
in the short-term,

00:07:38.760 --> 00:07:43.960
and insufficient data is available
for long-term safety.

00:07:43.960 --> 00:07:44.600
Finally today,

00:07:44.600 --> 00:07:46.960
we look at what behaviors
or circumstances

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:50.560
cause variability in the
onset of menopause.

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:52.240
Since 1970,

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:56.080
the proportion of women having
their first child after age 35

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:58.760
increased nearly tenfold.

00:07:58.760 --> 00:08:02.800
This may introduce a "longevity
penalty" on their children,

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:06.680
as those born to older mothers
don't tend to live as long,

00:08:06.680 --> 00:08:08.320
but mothers
having children later

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:10.920
tend to live longer themselves.

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:12.920
For example,
female centenarians

00:08:12.920 --> 00:08:15.120
were found to be
nearly four times more likely

00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:17.040
to have had children
after age 40

00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:19.840
than women
who died by their 70s.

00:08:19.840 --> 00:08:21.360
This doesn't necessarily mean

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:24.560
delaying kids
will make you live longer.

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:26.840
Smoking, for example,
could be a confounder,

00:08:26.840 --> 00:08:29.440
causing both early menopause
and an early death.

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:32.360
Or maybe
delayed reproductive aging

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:35.560
is just a sign
of slower aging in general.

00:08:35.560 --> 00:08:39.440
However some have suggested the
biological changes of pregnancy

00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:41.320
might have
a rejuvenating effect,

00:08:41.320 --> 00:08:45.480
even going so far as to suggest
that parabiosis mechanism,

00:08:45.480 --> 00:08:47.600
bathing in the blood of babies,

00:08:47.600 --> 00:08:50.760
but just not in
a Countess Bathory sort of way.

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:52.840
To sort between
these possibilities,

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:54.600
researchers studied
the longevity

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:58.400
of brothers of women
who gave birth after age 45,

00:08:58.400 --> 00:09:00.600
and that of their wives.

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:03.560
The brothers with late-fertile
sisters lived longer,

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:06.120
but their wives did not.

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:10.120
This suggests
a genetic robustness cause,

00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:12.320
rather than
a rejuvenation effect,

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:13.920
and the fact
that the longevity benefit

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:15.400
didn't extend to their wives

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:17.120
suggests it's not due
to a confounder

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:19.840
like socioeconomic strata.

00:09:19.840 --> 00:09:20.800
On the other hand,

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:24.240
women who experience
extremely early menopause,

00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:27.560
the 1% who stop menstruating
by age 39,

00:09:27.560 --> 00:09:30.600
may be at risk
for diminished longevity,

00:09:30.600 --> 00:09:31.880
and should
therefore be counseled

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:35.800
to adopt a particularly
healthy diet and lifestyle.

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:38.040
Approximately half
of the variability

00:09:38.040 --> 00:09:40.120
of age of menopause
between women

00:09:40.120 --> 00:09:42.640
is explained by genetics.

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:44.200
Other than smoking,

00:09:44.200 --> 00:09:46.560
what other behaviors
or circumstances

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:48.800
can help explain the rest?

00:09:48.800 --> 00:09:52.720
Factors that don't appear
to affect the age of menopause

00:09:52.720 --> 00:09:57.040
include exercise, obesity,
alcohol, coffee,

00:09:57.040 --> 00:09:59.440
or vitamin D status.

00:09:59.440 --> 00:10:02.440
Interestingly,
women who've been married

00:10:02.440 --> 00:10:05.040
tend to arrive
at menopause later.

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:08.400
Some suggested it may be the
influence of male pheromones,

00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:10.840
given the fact that exposure
to male armpit odor

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:13.640
makes women's cycles
more regular,

00:10:13.640 --> 00:10:16.520
but it turns out
that male cohabitation alone

00:10:16.520 --> 00:10:18.120
doesn't appear to matter.

00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:21.200
It may be the sex.

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:25.240
Married older individuals tend
to have more sex, and indeed,

00:10:25.240 --> 00:10:28.240
pre- and peri-menopausal women,
average age 46,

00:10:28.240 --> 00:10:29.320
who reported sex weekly

00:10:29.960 --> 00:10:33.200
were 28% less likely
to experience menopause

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:34.720
over the subsequent decade

00:10:34.720 --> 00:10:38.000
than those reporting sex
less than once a month.

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:41.040
You can very well imagine
how this could be a result

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:43.400
of reverse causation, though.

00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:46.080
Instead of more sex
leading to later menopause,

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:48.240
a later menopause
may have instead led

00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:50.120
to more sexual engagement.

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:53.880
The relationship between
tobacco use and early menopause

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:55.120
is thought to be mediated

00:10:55.120 --> 00:10:57.200
by the toxic effects
on the ovaries

00:10:57.200 --> 00:11:00.720
of the polycyclic aromatic
hydrocarbons in the smoke.

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:03.440
Among nonsmokers,

00:11:03.440 --> 00:11:07.400
this PAH exposure
is almost entirely from food,

00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:10.200
mostly grilled, barbequed,
and smoked meats.

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:11.400
Could this explain why,

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:13.800
in the Harvard Nurses'
Health Study II,

00:11:13.800 --> 00:11:15.960
higher plant protein intake
was associated

00:11:15.960 --> 00:11:19.160
with a significantly lower risk
of early menopause?

00:11:19.160 --> 00:11:21.780
Feed female monkeys
a diet high in animal protein

00:11:21.780 --> 00:11:24.560
and not only did they get
more atherosclerosis,

00:11:24.560 --> 00:11:28.120
but also an acceleration
of ovarian aging.

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:30.440
Now, in the original
Harvard Nurses' Health Study,

00:11:30.440 --> 00:11:33.160
animal protein consumption
was associated with infertility,

00:11:33.160 --> 00:11:35.640
such that replacing even 5%

00:11:35.640 --> 00:11:37.480
of animal protein intake
with plant protein

00:11:37.480 --> 00:11:40.640
could potentially cut the risk
of infertility in half.

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:42.640
But in
the Nurses' Health Study II,

00:11:42.640 --> 00:11:44.960
while plant protein
appeared to delay menopause,

00:11:44.960 --> 00:11:47.320
animal protein intake
was not associated

00:11:47.320 --> 00:11:49.560
with menopause age
either way.

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:51.560
And in
the UK Women's Cohort Study,

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:53.040
those eating more animal protein

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:57.040
were 6% more likely
to experience a later menopause.

00:11:57.040 --> 00:12:00.920
The data is similarly
conflicting in vegetarians.

00:12:00.920 --> 00:12:02.760
Some studies
found no difference

00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:05.760
or a later age of menopause
in vegetarians,

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:09.480
but others found an earlier age
compared to nonvegetarians.

00:12:09.480 --> 00:12:10.760
For example,
the largest study

00:12:10.760 --> 00:12:12.920
found that vegetarians
reached menopause

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:15.200
at an average age
of 50.1 years

00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:19.760
compared to nonvegetarians
at 50.7 years.

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:23.320
As I noted, premature menopause
before age 40

00:12:23.320 --> 00:12:25.520
may be detrimental
for longevity,

00:12:25.520 --> 00:12:28.040
but being a little earlier
within the normal range

00:12:28.040 --> 00:12:32.080
may actually be beneficial
for cancer risk.

00:12:32.080 --> 00:12:36.560
At the same age, breast cancer
risk is about 40% higher

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:40.120
in premenopausal compared
to postmenopausal women,

00:12:40.120 --> 00:12:41.720
presumably due
to higher exposure

00:12:41.720 --> 00:12:45.400
to the "necessary evil"
hormone estrogen.

00:12:45.400 --> 00:12:47.760
Breast cancer risk
is 3% higher

00:12:47.760 --> 00:12:50.600
for every year later
a woman starts menopause

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:53.280
and 5% higher
for every year earlier

00:12:53.280 --> 00:12:55.200
a girl starts menstruating.

00:12:55.200 --> 00:12:58.640
On average, women whose periods
hold off until age 15

00:12:58.640 --> 00:13:00.800
appear to live the longest.

00:13:00.800 --> 00:13:03.400
Vegetarian women tend to have
lower estrogen levels,

00:13:03.400 --> 00:13:05.480
perhaps due
to higher fiber intake,

00:13:05.480 --> 00:13:07.160
and interventional studies show

00:13:07.160 --> 00:13:08.680
that switching
to a more plant-based diet

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:10.560
can reduce
circulating estrogen levels

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:12.400
by more than 40%.

00:13:12.400 --> 00:13:14.440
This could explain
why vegetarian girls

00:13:14.440 --> 00:13:15.820
may hit puberty later,

00:13:15.820 --> 00:13:18.280
and why those eating
strictly vegetarian

00:13:18.280 --> 00:13:20.440
not only have
lower cancer risk overall,

00:13:20.440 --> 00:13:24.440
but particularly lower risk
for female-specific cancers.

00:13:24.440 --> 00:13:26.680
Age of menopause
may not be a factor though,

00:13:26.680 --> 00:13:28.640
based on
an interventional trial

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:31.000
randomizing women
on the verge of menopause,

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:32.440
average age 49,

00:13:32.440 --> 00:13:34.520
to two years
of a lower fat diet

00:13:34.520 --> 00:13:36.840
to reduce breast cancer risk.

00:13:36.840 --> 00:13:39.240
The intervention group
ended up eating more fiber,

00:13:39.240 --> 00:13:40.840
and therefore more plant-based,

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:42.840
but though they did
experience improvements

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:44.440
in mammogram findings,

00:13:44.440 --> 00:13:47.160
the dietary shift
failed to influence

00:13:47.160 --> 00:13:49.720
the timing of menopause.

